<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> In Pattern B, the number of small squares doubles from each step to the next.</item>
</list>
<para>Pattern B<figure><media alt="Four steps of a growing pattern. Step 0: One square. Step 1: Two squares, one atop the other. Step 2: Four squares in a two by two square. Step 3: Eight squares in a two by four rectangle."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e1178e6969e9b4d3ddc5767534e1ad9541129430"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Write an equation to represent the number of small squares at Step \(n\) in Pattern B. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(g(n)=2^n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Is the function in Pattern B, linear, quadratic, or exponential? </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>exponential</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> Complete the table for Pattern B. </item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
